Given: 2, 3, 6, 10, 17, ?

The logic followed here is:

The addition of the previous two differences, as shown below,

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/02a79792f7d3b89c8fc45c297562a07503cbe14aa0c1004b5a316ba300f372ca.png] 



2 + 1 = 3;

3 + 3 = 6;

6 + (1 + 3) = 6 + 4 = 10;

10 + (3 + 4) = 10 + 7 = 17;

17 + (4 + 7) = 17 + 11 = 28.

Hence, **28 ** is the correct answer.
